    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0497" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg425"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 20292/2–4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The President of the United States to the President of
                        Mexico.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >The White House</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June 25,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I have your courteous
                    note of June 16th,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d385-f1"/> sent me through Judge Wilfley
                    and thank you sincerely for your kindly attitude.</p>
                <p>I sincerely hope that in the course of a trip I hope to take in September and
                    October in the Southwest I may have the pleasure of meeting you at El Paso or
                    some convenient station at the border. It would gratify me very much to meet one
                    in the flesh who has done so much to establish order and create prosperity in
                    his own country and in so doing has won the admiration of the entire world.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. H. Taft.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
